# Privacy Policy — Bazaar Rush

**Last updated: 21 November 2026**

## 1. Introduction

Bazaar Rush is a mobile game developed and published by Ahmed Magdy Radwan ("Developer", "we", "us", or "our").

This Privacy Policy explains how information may be collected, used, shared, and processed when you play Bazaar Rush, including when you interact with advertisements.

We respect your privacy and aim to handle information responsibly and in accordance with applicable privacy laws.

## 2. Information We Collect

Bazaar Rush does not require you to create an account or provide your name, email address, or other directly identifying information to play the game.

However, third-party advertising services may collect or process information automatically, including:

- Advertising identifiers, such as the Android Advertising ID.
- Device information, such as device model, operating system, and language.
- IP address.
- Advertising interactions, including ad impressions, clicks, and rewarded ad completion.
- Diagnostics, fraud prevention, and advertising performance information.
- Consent and privacy preference information.

The information collected may depend on your device settings, consent choices, applicable laws, and the advertising services integrated into the game.

## 3. Advertising — Google AdMob

Bazaar Rush uses Google AdMob to display optional rewarded advertisements.

Rewarded advertisements may allow players to voluntarily receive in-game rewards, such as:

- Reviving their character after a game run.
- Doubling earned coins.
- Receiving optional in-game bonuses.

Watching advertisements is optional.

Google AdMob and its advertising partners may process information such as device identifiers, IP addresses, device information, and advertising interactions to deliver advertisements, measure advertising performance, prevent fraud, and provide personalized or non-personalized advertisements where permitted.

Google's processing of information is subject to Google's own privacy policies and terms.

Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

Google Advertising Technologies: https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads

## 4. How Information Is Used

Information processed by advertising providers may be used for:

- Displaying advertisements.
- Measuring advertising performance.
- Preventing fraud and abuse.
- Maintaining and improving advertising services.
- Providing personalized or non-personalized advertising where permitted.
- Complying with applicable legal requirements.

We do not use advertising data to deliberately manipulate game difficulty, collision probability, obstacle generation, or gameplay outcomes to force players to watch advertisements.

## 5. Consent and Privacy Choices

Where required by applicable laws, we provide consent and privacy preference mechanisms for advertising-related data processing.

Players may be presented with choices concerning personalized advertising and other applicable data processing purposes.

Where available, you may change or withdraw your consent through the privacy options provided within the game.

Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing that took place before consent was withdrawn.

If consent is not provided, certain advertising features may be limited or unavailable, or advertisements may be served under alternative permitted settings.

## 6. Legal Bases for Processing

Where applicable, personal data may be processed under the following legal bases:

- **Consent:** Where consent is required for advertising-related data processing.
- **Legitimate interests:** Where applicable, for security, fraud prevention, maintaining the game, and protecting the integrity of services, provided those interests do not override your rights.
- **Legal obligations:** Where processing is necessary to comply with applicable laws.

Third-party advertising providers may determine their own legal bases for certain processing activities.

## 7. Sharing of Information

We do not operate a user-account system or a personal user database as part of the game's core gameplay.

Information may be processed or shared by third-party advertising services, including Google AdMob and its advertising technology partners, as necessary for advertising delivery, measurement, fraud prevention, and other purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

Third-party providers may process information according to their own privacy policies and practices.

We do not sell personal information directly in exchange for money. However, certain advertising-related data sharing or processing may be considered "selling", "sharing", or targeted advertising under some privacy laws.

## 8. Data Retention

Game progress and settings may be stored locally on your device.

We do not maintain a personal user database or account records as part of the game's core gameplay, unless this changes in a future version.

Third-party advertising providers may retain information they collect according to their own retention policies, legal obligations, and business practices.

We do not control the retention periods of information independently processed by third-party advertising providers.

## 9. International Data Transfers

Third-party service providers, including Google, may process information in countries outside your country of residence.

Where applicable, appropriate safeguards may be used for international transfers of personal data in accordance with applicable data protection laws.

Please consult third-party privacy policies for additional information.

## 10. Your Privacy Rights

Depending on your country or state of residence, you may have rights regarding your personal information, including:

- The right to access personal information.
- The right to request correction of inaccurate information.
- The right to request deletion of personal information.
- The right to restrict certain processing activities.
- The right to object to certain processing activities.
- The right to withdraw consent.
- The right to request a copy of your information where applicable.
- The right to opt out of certain targeted advertising or data sharing where applicable.

To exercise rights concerning information for which we are responsible, contact us using the information in Section 14.

Some information may be processed directly by third-party advertising providers. In those cases, you may also need to exercise your rights directly with the relevant provider.

## 11. Children's Privacy

Bazaar Rush is not specifically designed for children under the age of 13.

The game does not currently require account registration or direct personal information submissions.

Advertising services may have additional age-related restrictions and privacy requirements.

If you believe personal information relating to a child has been processed inappropriately, please contact us so we can investigate.

Where required, we will implement appropriate age-related advertising restrictions and privacy protections.

## 12. Security

We and our service providers take reasonable measures to protect information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.

However, no method of electronic storage or transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

## 13. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes to the game, advertising services, legal requirements, or our privacy practices.

Any updated Privacy Policy will be published at the same URL with a revised update date.

